<title>UK: Quebec $1.0 bln 10-year bond due Tuesday - dealers.</title>
<headline>Quebec $1.0 bln 10-year bond due Tuesday - dealers.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quebec's expected $1.0 billion 10-year global bond could surface on Tuesday, syndicate managers said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;Quebec is likely to be launched tomorrow,&quot; said a syndicate head at a European bank. &quot;They will make a final decision this afternoon.&quot;</p>
<p>Spread talk was around 60 basis points over U.S. Treasury notes, dealers said.</p>
<p>Credit Suisse First Boston, Goldman Sachs and Merrill Lynch were tipped as bookrunners. There were likely to be two other joint lead managers in the deal, traders said.</p>
<p>-- Aline van Duyn, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
